---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { company } from "../data/company";

// Noindex, and excluded from the sitemap.
//
// The registered office and company number below are written out in full
// rather than pulled from company.ts. This is a legal document, and an edit
// to a data file should never be able to change what it says.
const hasEmail = Boolean(company.email);
const updated = "11 September 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | LeonEast Roofing & Building"
  description="How LeonEast Roofing & Building collects, uses and stores the personal information you provide when requesting a roof survey or quote."
  noindex={true}
>
  <section class="bg-carbon text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-mist">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 prose prose-neutral max-w-none">
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      This website is operated by LeonEast Roofing &amp; Building Limited, a company registered
      in England and Wales under number 16990741, whose registered office is at 132 Lewisham
      High Street, London, England, SE13 6EE. We work from {company.office.town},
      {company.county}. For the purposes of UK data protection law we are the data controller
      for the personal information described in this policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can contact us about anything in this policy by telephone on
      {" "}<a href={company.phoneLink}>{company.phone}</a>
      {hasEmail && <>, or by email at <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a></>}.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      When you submit an enquiry through this website, or contact us by phone, we collect the
      information you choose to give us. Typically that is your name, telephone number, email
      address, the property address the work relates to, and a description of the roofing
      problem. We do not ask for and do not want any special category data, and we do not
      collect payment details through this website.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our web forms are handled by Web3Forms, which passes the contents of the form to us by
      email. Our hosting provider records standard server information such as IP addresses and
      request logs for security and reliability purposes. We do not run advertising trackers,
      analytics cookies or third-party pixels on this site.
    </p>

    <h2>Why we use it, and our legal basis</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>To respond to your enquiry and arrange a survey.</strong> Legal basis: taking
        steps at your request prior to entering into a contract, and our legitimate interest in
        answering people who contact us.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>To prepare and issue a quotation, and to carry out work you accept.</strong>
        Legal basis: performance of a contract with you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>To keep records of work carried out, including survey and completion
        photographs, so that we can honour the workmanship guarantee.</strong> Legal basis:
        performance of a contract and our legitimate interest in being able to evidence what we
        did and when.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>To meet our legal and insurance obligations.</strong> Legal basis: compliance
        with a legal obligation, and our legitimate interests in defending claims.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We will not add you to a marketing list because you asked for a quote, and we do not sell
      or rent personal information to anyone.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>
      We share personal information only where it is necessary to do the job or to run the
      company. That may include our form provider and email provider, our website host, our
      accountant, our insurers, and - where you are making a claim - your own insurer or their
      loss adjuster. Where a job requires materials to be delivered to your address, the
      supplier will be given the delivery address. Each of these acts either as our processor
      under contract or as a controller in its own right.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Enquiries that do not lead to work are deleted within twelve months. Records relating to
      work we have carried out, including photographs and guarantee documentation, are kept for
      the length of the workmanship guarantee plus a further six years, which reflects the
      period in which a claim could be brought. Financial records are kept for six years as
      required for tax purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the UK GDPR you have the right to ask us for a copy of the personal information we
      hold about you, to have inaccurate information corrected, to ask us to delete information
      where we no longer need it, to restrict or object to certain processing, and to ask for
      your information in a portable format. Where we rely on legitimate interests you can
      object, and we will stop unless we have compelling grounds to continue.
    </p>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these, contact us using the details above. We will respond within one
      month. There is no charge.
    </p>

    <h2>Complaints</h2>
    <p>
      If you are unhappy with how we have handled your information, please tell us first so
      that we can try to put it right. You also have the right to complain to the Information
      Commissioner's Office, the UK supervisory authority, at
      {" "}<a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a>
      {" "}or on 0303 123 1113.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      This website does not set analytics, advertising or profiling cookies. Pages that embed a
      Google map load content from Google, which may set cookies of its own under Google's
      privacy policy; where a map is embedded it is clearly visible on the page.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of the page shows when
      it was last changed.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
